\begin{center}
{\Large\itshape\color{CoverGoldBright} וַאֲנִי בַּיהוָה אֶעְלוֹזָה אָגִילָה בֵּאלֹהֵי יִשְׁעִי}\\[0.1cm]
{\itshape\small\color{CoverMuted} {\baskervillefont "Yet I will exult in the LORD, I will rejoice in the God of my salvation"} · 全書最後的轉折 (3:18)}

\vspace{0.4cm}

\fleuron[CoverGoldBright]\hspace{0.25cm}{\color{CoverGoldBright}\rule{1.8in}{0.4pt}}\hspace{0.25cm}\fleuron[CoverGoldBright]

\vspace{0.4cm}

{\large\bfseries\color{CoverCream} 關於本書}\qquad{\baskervillefont\itshape\large\color{CoverGoldBright} About This Book}

\vspace{0.4cm}

\begin{minipage}{5in}
\small\color{CoverCream}
哈巴谷書只有三章五十六節，是一場先知與神之間的禱告對話：先知兩次發問，神兩次回答，最後以一首要交給伶長的歌收尾。全書的骨架是三個動詞——先知控告神「不聽」「不救」，又「使我看見」惡（1:2-3）；到第三章，這三個動詞全部回來：我聽見了、拯救、我看見了。問題沒有被解釋掉，先知被帶到另一個地方站著：然而，我要因耶和華歡欣。本書分五步逐節研讀全卷，以「啟示的次序」為骨幹，整合老弟兄的查經方法、加爾文與亨利的歷代注疏，以及 G. Campbell Morgan 的解經。每一句歸給注疏家的引文都附英文原文與出處，可以按圖索驥核對。

\vspace{0.3cm}

{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream}\lettrine[lines=3,findent=2pt,nindent=2pt]{\color{CoverGoldBright}H}{}abakkuk has three chapters and fifty-six verses, yet it is a single conversation of prayer: the prophet asks twice, God answers twice, and the book closes with a song handed to the choirmaster. Its frame is three verbs. The prophet charges God with not hearing and not saving, and with making him see wickedness (1:2-3); in chapter 3 all three verbs come back: I have heard, salvation, I saw. The question is not explained away; the prophet is led to another place to stand: yet I will rejoice in the LORD. This study reads the whole book in five movements, built on the order of revelation, with Elder Wong's way of reading Scripture, the commentary of John Calvin and Matthew Henry, and G. Campbell Morgan's exposition. Every quotation attributed to a commentator is given in its original English with a source a reader can check.}
\end{minipage}

\vspace{0.4cm}

{\small\bfseries\color{CoverCream} 五步：從控告到歡欣}\qquad{\baskervillefont\itshape\small\color{CoverGoldBright} Five Movements}

\vspace{0.3cm}

\begin{minipage}{4.7in}
\small\color{CoverCream}
\begin{tabular}{@{}cp{3.4in}l@{}}
第一步 & 先知先開口 \textit{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream} The cry: how long?} & {\tiny\color{CoverMuted} 1:1-4}\\[0.25em]
第二步 & 回答比問題更大 \textit{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream} A work you would not believe} & {\tiny\color{CoverMuted} 1:5-11}\\[0.25em]
第三步 & 再問，然後上守望所 \textit{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream} I will stand at my watch} & {\tiny\color{CoverMuted} 1:12-2:1}\\[0.25em]
第四步 & 寫下、等候、因信得生 \textit{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream} The vision and the woes} & {\tiny\color{CoverMuted} 2:2-20}\\[0.25em]
第五步 & 聽見、看見、歡欣 \textit{\baskervillefont\color{CoverCream} The song of the watchman} & {\tiny\color{CoverMuted} 3:1-19}\\
\end{tabular}
\end{minipage}

\vspace{0.4cm}

{\color{CoverGoldBright}\rule{2.3in}{0.6pt}}

\vspace{0.25cm}

{\normalsize\itshape\color{CoverCream} 雖然遲延，還要等候；因為必然臨到，不再遲延。}\\
{\baskervillefont\footnotesize\itshape\color{CoverMuted} "Though it tarries, wait for it; For it will certainly come, it will not delay." — Habakkuk 2:3}

